    sha256: 0474580014a697c47370992feee115d49c80b105b9c43270bf89afff0e4b0aa5
  body: "# Benefit-specific remunerative work and treated cases\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    chapter combines work hours, payment or expected payment and benefit-specific claimant/partner scope,
    while distinguishing actual remunerative work from cases treated as in or not in it.\n\n## Scope and
    exceptions\n\nJSA(Cont), JSA(IB) and IS must remain distinct. The selected hours passages are source
    context, not a complete present-day threshold rule: fluctuations, averaging, treated cases, exceptions
    and joint claims require further evidence. The definitions must not be applied to UC or New Style
    JSA by analogy.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 20201, PDF page 46](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=46)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20202, PDF page 46](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=46)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20210, PDF page 49](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=49)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20212, PDF page 50](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=50)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20213, PDF page 50](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=50)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n- [DMG 20214, PDF page 50](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/67ffaf91694d57c6b1cf8e0e/dmgch20.pdf#page=50)
    — DMG Vol 4: Ch 20, JSA and IS, conditions of entitlement.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review
    is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring
    time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document,
    individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter
    reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural
    evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch20`: PDF SHA-256 `0474580014a697c47370992feee115d49c80b105b9c43270bf89afff0e4b0aa5`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `ed007251fa43ff9c63f5116f603798f2279c84006af8539bbbfd50194ab0ab56`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsa-personal-rate
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The work condition is claimant-only for JSA(Cont), consistent with its
      personal-benefit scope; the means-tested provisions separately include a partner.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch20/0046
      quote: "20201 JSA(Cont) is a personal benefit and is not payable for a partner 1. The remunerative
        work exclusion\ntherefore applies only to the claimant.\n\n\n                                \
        \                                                            1 JS Act 95, s 4(1)\n\n\n\nJSA(IB)
        and IS"
      locator: DMG 20201
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch20/0046
      quote: "20202 The remunerative work exclusion applies where the person engaged in remunerative work
        is the\n\n\n1. claimant or\n\n\n2. claimant’s partner, if the claimant is a member of a couple.\n\
        \n\n\nDoes the claimant have employment"
      locator: DMG 20202
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-continuing-work
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source requires a factual continuing-work finding before the hours assessment.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch20/0046
      quote: "20200 [See Memo DMG 13/20] Being in remunerative work affects entitlement to JSA and IS
        1. In all\ncases, before the DM applies the law to establish how many hours a person is working,
        they must decide\nwhether or not the work is continuing.\n\n\n                               \
        \                               1 JS Act 95, s 1(2)(e); SS CB Act 92, s 124(1)(c)\n\n\n\nJSA(Cont)"
      locator: DMG 20200
